From: Project contributors <contributors@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] dae-core: splice XTLS Vision flows after the direct switch

dae chooses a relay path once, when the relay starts. A Vision conn does
not unwrap to *net.TCPConn, so its flows always took relayCopyLoop, and
kept copying both directions through userspace after Vision had switched
them to the raw socket (inner TLS 1.3, which is most proxied traffic).

relayCopyLoop now checks, between chunks and only when one end is a
netproxy.DirectTCPConnProvider, whether both ends of its direction
resolve to raw sockets. When they do, the direction continues with the
splice(2) loop of the fast path (relaySpliceTCPPair, split out of
relayFastCopy unchanged), with the same traffic records, activity
refreshes, deadlines and half-close. Bytes that a LAN-side sniffing
wrapper still buffers are written first, as tryRelayGatherWrite does.
The sockmap offload and its opt-in are unchanged.

See docs/dae-kernel-proxy-study.md, option A.
---
Index: daed-2.1.1/dae-core/control/tcp_copy_engine.go
===================================================================
--- daed-2.1.1.orig/dae-core/control/tcp_copy_engine.go
+++ daed-2.1.1/dae-core/control/tcp_copy_engine.go
@@ -68,12 +68,22 @@ func (defaultRelayCopyEngine) Copy(ctx context.Context, dst netproxy.Conn, src n
 func relayCopyLoop(ctx context.Context, dst netproxy.Conn, src netproxy.Conn, buf []byte, record func(int64), onActive func(int64)) (written int64, err error) {
 	record = normalizeTrafficRecord(record)
 	onActive = normalizeTrafficRecord(onActive)
+	handover := relayDirectHandoverCandidate(dst, src)
 	for {
 		// Check context cancellation. relayCore.run ensures ctx is never nil.
 		if cerr := ctx.Err(); cerr != nil {
 			return written, cerr
 		}
 
+		// Between chunks buf is empty, so once both ends of this direction
+		// resolve to raw sockets (XTLS Vision after its direct switch) the
+		// rest of the direction can move to splice(2) without reordering.
+		if handover {
+			if n, err, ok := tryRelayDirectHandover(ctx, dst, src, record, onActive); ok {
+				return written + n, err
+			}
+		}
+
 		nr, er := src.Read(buf)
 		if nr > 0 {
 			onActive(int64(nr))
